            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"N0Dfd70vKo3C16x22MllfNEwg8e\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-GtR1dyOpDoA3mHxnp60lZSYxgVf\">On the other hand, despite being the dominant industry in 1930, with approximately 75% of the labour force employed in farming, fishing and foresting, this sector saw a dramatic drop over the years, reaching a low of only 5% in 2010. Finally, the percentage of workers in other services rose from 10% to 15% in the first decade, then then fell back to a relatively stable level of around 10% for the rest of the period.</div>\n</div>",
